            <ArticleTitle>Atypical primary headache responding to finger pressure: possible involvement of the vagus nerve?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of atypical primary headache strongly responsive to prolonged pressure in the anterior aspect of the neck. We hypothesize that, at least in this case, the trigemino-cervical system and its connections with the vagus nerve are involved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
